 0, Entry Helix radius 1.
 
+**Pass starts at** (Passes tab) sets where each level starts:
+
+- **Auto** cuts the rings from the middle of the area outward. This is
+  the order that 2D Offset always cut.
+- **Outside** starts at the outer edge of the area and works in. With an
+  Outside containment, the outer edge is the stock edge: the tool starts
+  outside the stock, cuts one stepover at a time and ends on the part
+  wall. Use it to stop full-width slots in the stock.
+- **Inside** starts at the part or island wall and works out.
+
 **Do not touch** (Geometry tab, **Boundaries**): pick faces or edge chains
 to protect from every cut, plunge, ramp, helix, keep-down and rapid link
 across the full tool assembly (flutes, shank and holder). **Clearance**

From 8e6bb98751ec24a35b547e75c2b24d6632b7b082 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mkinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 12:38:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] fix(2d): Pass starts at (Auto/Inside/Outside) for Bore

Bore takes the shared pass_start parameter of #3316. The ring ladder of
each level is ordered by PassStart::rank through the new motion entry
bore_started. Auto keeps the centre-out walk byte for byte. Outside cuts
the wall ring first and walks in. Inside is the centre-out order, because
a hole has no inner wall.

The field rides EditOperationParams, the MCP edit_operation door and the
project key pass_start (auto never written). The Bore Passes tab shows the
shared row with a Bore hint.

Stacked on #3353.

Fixes #3360

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
