+**Pass starts at** sets the order of the rings at each level. **Auto**
+cuts from the centre out and ends on the wall. A hole has no inner wall,
+so **Inside** is the same order. **Outside** cuts the wall ring first and
+then works in to the centre. Each level still starts with the dive at the
+centre.
+
 **Common refusals:** "boring needs at least one hole"; "clearance plane
 below a hole entry".
 

From 319a074ec28f7b98e9027c371f5afcca98ed8cc8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mkinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:48:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] refactor(motion): name the Bore pass order parameter
 pass_start

The ring loop binds its own `start` point, so the parameter of
bore_started reads as pass_start. No behaviour change.

Refs #3360

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
